61_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T04:29:48-07:00","id":1516630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1507333-favorite-movie-genres?p=1516542#post1516542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it will be closer to the Brandon Lee movie myself Mr. Gone, but you could be right and it will be closer to the comic and RIP Brandon Lee and Michael Massie from that film.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of hope it's not just a remake of the original. Plus, it'd be hard to top that one, it's sooo good!<br /> <br /> And yea, Brandon Lee and Michael Massie were awesome and they're definitely missed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1507333-favorite-movie-genres?p=1516544#post1516544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, the rumors about a Crow remake pop up every few years. Don\u2019t get me wrong, if one does come out it could have the worst cast in the world and I\u2019d still be there opening day.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Not sure if this means much, but here's some articles about the new one, assuming it actually comes out:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://collider.com/the-crow-reboot-cast-director-filming/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://static0.colliderimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/the-crow-reboot-poster.jpg?w=1200&amp;h=675&amp;fit=crop\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://collider.com/the-crow-reboot-cast-director-filming/\" target=\"_blank\"> 'The Crow': Release Date, Cast, Plot, and Everything We Know About the Long-Delayed Reboot </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://collider.com/the-crow-reboot-cast-director-filming/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://collider.com/the-crow-reboot-cast-director-filming/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> After 15 years of languishing in development, 'The Crow' reboot is almost here. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://movieweb.com/the-crow-reboot-officially-in-post-production-gets-new-financial-backer/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://static0.moviewebimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/Bill-Skarsgard-Crow-Fan-ARt.jpg?w=1200&amp;h=675&amp;fit=crop\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://movieweb.com/the-crow-reboot-officially-in-post-production-gets-new-financial-backer/\" target=\"_blank\"> The Crow Reboot Officially in Post-Production With New Financial Backer </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://movieweb.com/the-crow-reboot-officially-in-post-production-gets-new-financial-backer/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://movieweb.com/the-crow-reboot-officially-in-post-production-gets-new-financial-backer/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> After all these years, it looks like we may really, actually, finally be getting a reboot of The Crow. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So, it seems it's actually happening... but I guess we'll see. I'll be curious about it..<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1507333-favorite-movie-genres?p=1516546#post1516546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've watched the original Crow with Brandon Lee, the not so good follow up and a third one with Kristan Dunst in it and I heard that they made one with Edward Furlong, David Borenz and I think Tara Reid in it but I never bothered to watch it. Nothing beats the original film in my regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>The second one, City of Angels isn't too bad. It's not great, but not completely horrible. The third one is pretty good all things considered and I'm glad they tried to do something a little different. That 4th one with Edward Furlong is awful! And not even like funny bad, it's just baad.<br /> <br /> There was a Crow TV show that was pretty good too, all things considered. Mark Dacasos plays Eric Draven in it. They change the mythology just a bit, but for a tv series I can understand why. If you've never seen it I recommend it!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T06:01:55-07:00","id":1516636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1507333-favorite-movie-genres?p=1516546#post1516546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've watched the original Crow with Brandon Lee, the not so good follow up and a third one with Kristan Dunst in it and I heard that they made one with Edward Furlong, David Borenz and I think Tara Reid in it but I never bothered to watch it. Nothing beats the original film in my regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>The one with Edward Furlong was definitely B-Movie/Grindhouse cheesy but it was fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T09:21:07-07:00","id":1516660,"title":"","content":"I totally forgot about the short lived tv series about Crow.",